depgraph: raise the garbage collector threshold during backtrack_depgraph

Alone on 3.0.83: start 119.6 -> 116.1, masks 91.0 -> 89.2. Changes only
when unreachable cycles are freed.
Patches 0001-0009 together, sum of six states: 447.5 -> 239.6 s (-46 %):
  start 63.2, holds 26.4, masks 48.8, py313 40.0, bdeps 34.5, policykit 26.7
Applies to upstream head unchanged.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
---
--- a/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
+++ b/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 import collections
 import errno
 import functools
+import gc
 import json
 import logging
 import os
@@ -12605,12 +12606,20 @@
     backtracked, max_retries = -1, -1
     start_time = time.monotonic()
     _start_resolution_display(spinner, myopts)
+    # The resolver allocates container objects much faster than it frees
+    # them, so with the default threshold the cyclic garbage collector runs
+    # every 2000 net allocations and its full collections walk the whole heap
+    # again and again. This only changes when unreachable cycles are freed.
+    gc_threshold = gc.get_threshold()
+    if 0 < gc_threshold[0] < 500000:
+        gc.set_threshold(500000, *gc_threshold[1:])
     try:
         success, mydepgraph, favorites, backtracked, max_retries = _backtrack_depgraph(
             settings, trees, myopts, myparams, myaction, myfiles, spinner
         )
         return (success, mydepgraph, favorites)
     finally:
+        gc.set_threshold(*gc_threshold)
         if spinner is not None and spinner.end_notice():
             _show_resolution_report(start_time, backtracked, max_retries)
 
